digest="f8cfb6312c0c285819af1bddd61508e1a0dfc08de179d1625c02eab8f2b7e08d">src/review/command.ts</File><File digest="30f5b984e431252490a3d4b3b4eeba756f007a93e145fc2a60aed8dc4782d498">src/review/core.test.ts</File><File digest="b822f8728ecf0a41385de0590a8ad2b594d19da62fd08363afe880d3d4fdbedc">src/review/core.ts</File></WriteEvidence></Event><Event id="18" task="T-006" kind="terminal" /></Epoch-1><Verdicts><Verdict outcome="pass" scope="bundle" classification="implementation">Reviewed against the approved spec by the authority. Review 0 findings; WriteEvidence scope audit 23 paths 0 findings; attempt-pair audit 5 pairs 0 findings; scope audit not-run on a clean tree, the honest F27 case. Verified independently: suite 1495 pass 3 skip 0 fail, validate:ci exit 0, REVIEW_ISSUE_SEVERITIES is a three-member runtime const, and no AC-SUITE-AND-LINT element exists in either artifact.

DISCLOSURE 1, THE STEP'S CENTRAL CLAUSE WAS REFUTED AND NOTHING WAS DEMOTED. P2.5 said that after items 1 to 4, remaining low-value change-meta findings would be demoted to info so the default view is signal. That sentence was written before any of 1 to 4 existed. Measured at this HEAD: unscoped review reports zero findings and ten archived bundles are clean with both audits run; the only phrase-matching codes are two lint warnings this bundle must not touch. Demoting anything would have hidden signal rather than noise, in the phase whose subject is review honesty. The demotion set is empty and that is the finding, not a shortfall.

DISCLOSURE 2, THE PHASE SUCCESS METRIC IS NOT EVIDENCEABLE HERE AND IS NOT A CRITERION. P2 states up front that scope findings must drop at least eighty percent on the corpus's own transcripts while every planted violation is still caught. Those transcripts are citations in review.md, not trees in this repository. A percentage measured against an absent artifact fails D16, and putting it in an acceptance criterion would be the theater this phase keeps recording. The planted-violation half is in-repo and is AC-DETECTION. The percentage is recorded here as disclosure and re-entry belongs to a later fixture bundle if those trees ever become artifacts.

DISCLOSURE 3, TWO GAPS IN THE SPEC I APPROVED, BOTH NAMED BY THE EXECUTOR RATHER THAN PAPERED OVER. First: AC-HEAD-RED should have exempted the constructed-info matrix the way it exempted AC-DETECTION, because runReview cannot exhibit dropping info at HEAD without an emitter the same spec forbids. The executor split it - the recorded filter red is an error threshold dropping a live warning, the constructed matrix is pass-side - which is closable and honest, and the report states plainly that the filter red does not evidence dropping info. Second: ReviewIssueSeverity is a type-only union with no runtime referent, verified, so a third value is erased and deleteable by exactly the cleanup this bundle was meant to prevent. REVIEW_ISSUE_SEVERITIES is the executor's patch, not the spec's, and both the refusal message and the threshold read it.

DISCLOSURE 4, THE REFUSAL RED AVOIDS SELLING AN EARLIER BUNDLE'S REPAIR. An unrecognised severity token already exits 1 today because C-RECORDED-DEBT made unknown arguments refuse. A CLI red observing only the exit code would have evidenced that repair rather than this property. The refusal is tested in-process through resolveReviewSeverity after the flag is declared, never spawning the CLI and never asserting on exit codes.

DISCLOSURE 5, F85 AND SIX DISCHARGES. The executor found my dispatch citing F76 as a live trap when C-RECORDED-DEBT had already delivered it, because no finding in this ledger had ever been marked discharged. F85 records the rule - append a discharge line at the close that pays a finding, and read a finding's last line before citing it. Six findings were annotated append-only: F60, F71, F74, F76, F77 and F82. F74.2 and F84 remain genuinely owed and are named as such.

DISCLOSURE 6, TWO PLAN DEFECTS THE EXECUTOR REPAIRED AND REPORTED. The T-005 README pin implied the as-row's unbracketed flag matcher, which cannot match the optional-bracket spelling this README already uses for change and base; repaired to a matcher that still binds the first Overview cell of a review row rather than a free README needle. And the T-001 production bullet sequenced the MODULE_MAP update one trip too late - once the extract exports the name, an unmapped export is a second signature - so the map moved with the extract.

DISCLOSURE 7, INSTALLED SKILLS WERE DRIFTED ON EIGHT SKILLS AND WERE REFRESHED BEFORE WORK BEGAN, at the user's instruction. The executor had reported that drift on nearly every dispatch in this phase; telling it the repo copy wins each time treated the symptom. Note that refreshing does not resolve F84: the shipped ngrace-execute still assigns final assertions, apply and archive to the executor while this roadmap's close is authority-owned, and that remains a product decision owed.

DISCLOSURE 8, WHAT REMAINS UNPINNED. runReview dropping info has no live emitter, so it is exercised only through the pass-side constructed matrix. The corpus percentage is absent as above. Post-archive lint 0/0 is verdict evidence, not a task criterion, per the F82 repair this phase adopted. No new path emission, so CI remains the only observer of separators.

DISCLOSURE 9. decisions.md was written during the open window - F85 and the six discharge annotations - each in its own commit ahead of the implementation commit, staged by filename rather than with add -A. It is outside every bundle's ObservedWriteScope by design, and the scope audit reads working-tree porcelain, so committing removed those edits from the audit's view rather than clearing them.</Verdict></Verdicts><Decisions><Decision gate="apply" decision="permit"><Requirement id="plan-present" required="true" present="true" blocking="false">status=approved</Requirement><Requirement id="no-unresolved-satisfied-ac-clarification" required="true" present="true" blocking="false" /><Requirement id="review-verdict" required="true" present="true" blocking="false">outcome=pass</Requirement></Decision><Decision gate="archive" decision="permit"><Requirement id="no-open-epoch" required="true" present="true" blocking="false">run/ empty</Requirement></Decision></Decisions></C-FINDING-SEVERITIES></NgraceRunLedger>
